WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:18.417
Multiply out one plus x, cubed, and it stops. But the square root of one plus x never stops. A binomial expansion rewrites a bracket to a power as a sum of powers of x. Ascending means smallest power first.

00:00:19.000 --> 00:00:32.934
Here is the formula. One plus X, to the n, is one, plus n X, plus n times n minus one over two factorial, times X squared, and so on. Three factorial is three times two times one, which is six.

00:00:33.520 --> 00:00:46.740
Rewrite roots and fractions as powers. The root of one minus four x is one minus four x, to the power a half. One over one plus three x, squared, is one plus three x, to the minus two.

00:00:47.320 --> 00:00:57.103
X is the whole second term, with its sign and number. For one minus four x, X is minus four x. So X squared is sixteen x squared.

00:00:57.680 --> 00:01:04.053
So you get a root, fraction or negative power, and expand up to a stated power of x, term by term.

00:01:05.160 --> 00:01:16.080
Step one: write one plus something, to a power. Step two: find n and X. The formula only works when the bracket starts with one.

00:01:16.640 --> 00:01:24.751
Step three: write each term with X in brackets. Step four: simplify each coefficient, watching the signs.

00:01:25.320 --> 00:01:31.348
The trap is squaring only the x. Minus four x, squared, is sixteen x squared.

00:01:32.480 --> 00:01:46.849
January twenty twenty. Expand the square root of one minus four x in ascending powers of x, up to and including the x cubed term. Each coefficient is an integer. Three marks.

00:01:47.400 --> 00:01:57.652
Step one: rewrite as a power. The root is one minus four x, to the power one half. So n is a half, and X is minus four x.

00:01:58.240 --> 00:02:09.780
Step two: write the terms with brackets. The coefficients use a half, minus a half, and minus three halves. The last is divided by six.

00:02:10.360 --> 00:02:24.079
Step three: simplify. A half times minus four x is minus two x. Minus one eighth times sixteen is minus two. One sixteenth times minus sixty four is minus four.

00:02:24.640 --> 00:02:34.786
A tempting wrong route squares only the x. That gives plus a half x squared, which is wrong. The correct term is minus two x squared.

00:02:35.360 --> 00:02:53.136
So the expansion is one, minus two x, minus two x squared, minus four x cubed. A quick check: x equal to nought point nought one gives about nought point nine eight, the same as the root of nought point nine six. This explanation is by olevels dot com, not an official mark scheme.

00:02:54.240 --> 00:03:05.623
A common mistake is a sign slip. Do not guess the pattern. Work each sign out term by term, from n minus one, n minus two, and from X.

00:03:06.760 --> 00:03:25.854
Now you try, from November twenty twenty. Expand one plus p x, to the power minus five, in ascending powers of x, up to the term in x to the fourth. Simplest form. Three marks. Write your answer, then choose Continue to Answer.

00:03:26.960 --> 00:03:36.084
Here n is minus five, and X is p x. The coefficients are one, minus five, fifteen, minus thirty five, and seventy.

00:03:36.640 --> 00:03:48.479
Now raise p x to each power. The terms are one, minus five p x, plus fifteen p squared x squared, minus thirty five p cubed x cubed, plus seventy p to the fourth x to the fourth.

00:03:49.040 --> 00:03:56.180
The common wrong answer squares only the x, giving fifteen p x squared. The p needs the same power.

00:03:56.760 --> 00:04:03.556
Remember: write a power, find n and X, use the formula with brackets, then simplify every term.
